<div class="report">

<div class="report-header">
  <div class="tag">Trend Analysis Report</div>
  <h1>BIEK Computer Science 12th Class<br>Past Paper Analysis (2015–2025)</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">A comprehensive trend analysis of question types, frequency patterns, and topic distribution across 11 years of BIEK Computer Science HSC Part-2 examination papers.</p>
  <p class="meta">Generated: May 7, 2026 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Dataset: 327 questions &nbsp;|&nbsp; Source: BIEK Official Past Papers</p>
</div>

<div class="report-body">

<!-- TOC -->
<div class="toc">
  <h3>Table of Contents</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><a href="#overview">Dataset &amp; Examination Overview</a></li>
    <li><a href="#yearly-distribution">Year-by-Year Question Volume Analysis</a></li>
    <li><a href="#question-type-analysis">Question Type Composition &amp; Trends</a></li>
    <li><a href="#topic-patterns">Recurring Topics &amp; Question Content Patterns</a></li>
    <li><a href="#exam-prep-insights">Strategic Insights for Exam Preparation</a></li>
    <li><a href="#conclusions">Conclusions &amp; Limitations</a></li>
  </ol>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 1: OVERVIEW -->
<h2 id="overview">1. Dataset &amp; Examination Overview</h2>

<p>This analysis draws on a community-compiled question bank of <strong>327 Computer Science questions</strong> from BIEK 12th Class (HSC Part-2) examinations spanning the 11-year period from 2015 to 2025. Each row represents a single examination question categorized by type &mdash; <strong>MCQs</strong> (Multiple Choice Questions), <strong>Short</strong> (short-answer), or <strong>Long</strong> (essay-type questions with sub-parts).</p>

<div class="kpi-grid">
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-value">327</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Total Questions Analyzed</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-value">10</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Years with Data Available</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card warn">
    <div class="kpi-value">1</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Missing Year (2020)</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-value">3</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Question Types (MCQ, Short, Long)</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="caution-box">
  <strong>Important Note:</strong> The year <strong>2020</strong> is absent from this dataset. This is consistent with the COVID-19 pandemic, during which BIEK examinations were either cancelled, postponed, or conducted under an alternative assessment model. All analyses and year-over-year comparisons skip 2020. The 2015&ndash;2025 range is treated as 10 data-bearing years.
</div>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Question Type</th><th class="num">Count</th><th class="num">Share of Total</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>MCQs</td><td class="num">150</td><td class="num">45.9%</td><td>Multiple choice, four options, separated by $ delimiter</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Short</td><td class="num">147</td><td class="num">45.0%</td><td>Short-answer, definitions, program writing, conversions</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Long</td><td class="num">30</td><td class="num">9.2%</td><td>Essay-type with multiple sub-parts ($-delimited)</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>The dataset is nearly balanced between MCQs and Short Questions (45.9% vs. 45.0%), with Long Questions making up the remaining 9.2%. This reflects the typical BIEK exam pattern where the paper includes a fixed MCQ section alongside short-answer and essay sections.</p>

<!-- SECTION 2: YEARLY DISTRIBUTION -->
<h2 id="yearly-distribution">2. Year-by-Year Question Volume Analysis</h2>

<p>One of the most striking findings is the <strong>stair-step pattern</strong> in total question counts across the decade. Rather than gradual evolution, the exam structure shifted in discrete jumps between three stable configurations.</p>

<div class="era-box">
  <h4>Three Structural Eras Identified</h4>
  <div class="era-grid">
    <div class="era-item">
      <div class="era-years">2015 &ndash; 2016</div>
      <div class="era-detail">Early Phase<br><strong>27 questions</strong><br>15 MCQ + 9 Short + 3 Long</div>
    </div>
    <div class="era-item">
      <div class="era-years">2017 &ndash; 2019</div>
      <div class="era-detail">Expanded Phase<br><strong>36 questions</strong><br>15 MCQ + 18 Short + 3 Long</div>
    </div>
    <div class="era-item">
      <div class="era-years">2021 &ndash; 2025</div>
      <div class="era-detail">Stabilized Phase<br><strong>33 questions</strong><br>15 MCQ + 15 Short + 3 Long</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="chart-box">
  <div class="chart-title">Total Question Count by Year (Stacked by Type)</div>
  <canvas id="chartYearlyStacked"></canvas>
</div>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th class="num">MCQs</th><th class="num">Short</th><th class="num">Long</th><th class="num">Total</th><th class="num">YoY Change</th><th class="num">YoY %</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>2015</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">9</td><td class="num">3</td><td class="num"><strong>27</strong></td><td class="num">&mdash;</td><td class="num">&mdash;</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2016</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">9</td><td class="num">3</td><td class="num"><strong>27</strong></td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">0.0%</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2017</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">18</td><td class="num">3</td><td class="num"><strong>36</strong></td><td class="num" style="color:#16a34a">+9</td><td class="num" style="color:#16a34a">+33.3%</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2018</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">18</td><td class="num">3</td><td class="num"><strong>36</strong></td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">0.0%</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2019</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">18</td><td class="num">3</td><td class="num"><strong>36</strong></td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">0.0%</td></tr>
    <tr style="background:#fef2f2"><td>2020</td><td class="num" colspan="6" style="text-align:center;color:#dc2626">No data available (COVID-19 pandemic disruption)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2021</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">3</td><td class="num"><strong>33</strong></td><td class="num" style="color:#dc2626">&minus;3</td><td class="num" style="color:#dc2626">&minus;8.3%</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2022</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">3</td><td class="num"><strong>33</strong></td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">0.0%</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2023</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">3</td><td class="num"><strong>33</strong></td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">0.0%</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2024</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">3</td><td class="num"><strong>33</strong></td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">0.0%</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2025</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">3</td><td class="num"><strong>33</strong></td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">0.0%</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Key Observations</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>MCQ count is invariant:</strong> Exactly 15 MCQs appear in every single year from 2015 to 2025. This is the most rigid structural element of the exam.</li>
  <li><strong>Long question count is invariant:</strong> Exactly 3 long-form questions appear every year, never varying.</li>
  <li><strong>Short questions are the only variable:</strong> All structural change in the exam is driven entirely by adjustments to the Short Question count: 9 (2015&ndash;2016), 18 (2017&ndash;2019), 15 (2021&ndash;2025).</li>
  <li><strong>Post-pandemic contraction:</strong> After 2020, the exam settled at 33 questions &mdash; 3 fewer than the 2017&ndash;2019 peak. This may reflect a deliberate post-pandemic adjustment.</li>
  <li><strong>Five-year stability:</strong> The 2021&ndash;2025 block shows perfect year-to-year stability (zero change for five consecutive years), suggesting the current format is well-established.</li>
</ul>

<!-- SECTION 3: QUESTION TYPE ANALYSIS -->
<h2 id="question-type-analysis">3. Question Type Composition &amp; Trends</h2>

<p>While absolute counts reveal structural shifts, the <strong>proportional composition</strong> tells a richer story about the relative emphasis placed on each question format over time.</p>

<div class="chart-box">
  <div class="chart-title">Question Type Proportion Trends (2015&ndash;2025)</div>
  <canvas id="chartProportions"></canvas>
</div>

<div class="chart-box">
  <div class="chart-title">Short Question Count &mdash; The Only Variable Component</div>
  <canvas id="chartShortVariation"></canvas>
</div>

<p>The MCQ share of the total paper has followed a U-shaped trajectory:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>2015&ndash;2016:</strong> MCQs represented 55.6% of all questions &mdash; the highest MCQ dominance in the dataset.</li>
  <li><strong>2017&ndash;2019:</strong> MCQ share dropped to 41.7% as Short Questions doubled from 9 to 18, shifting the exam toward written-response assessment.</li>
  <li><strong>2021&ndash;2025:</strong> MCQ share partially recovered to 45.5% as Short Questions were reduced to 15, creating the current balanced configuration.</li>
</ul>

<p>Long Questions have remained consistently at 8.3&ndash;11.1% of the total across all years &mdash; a remarkably stable component that anchors the exam structure.</p>

<div class="kpi-grid">
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-value">15.0</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Avg. MCQs per Year (min 15, max 15)</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-value">14.7</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Avg. Short Qs per Year (min 9, max 18)</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-value">3.0</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Avg. Long Qs per Year (min 3, max 3)</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-value">32.7</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Avg. Total Qs per Year (min 27, max 36)</div>
  </div>
</div>

<h3>Stability Assessment</h3>
<p>The BIEK Computer Science exam exhibits <strong>segmented stability</strong>: the MCQ and Long Question sections are essentially fixed, while the Short Question section serves as the adjustment lever. This is a deliberate design feature &mdash; it allows the board to expand or contract the exam's depth while preserving core structural elements. The current 33-question format (2021&ndash;2025) has remained unchanged for <strong>five consecutive years</strong>, the longest stable period in the dataset.</p>

<!-- SECTION 4: TOPIC PATTERNS -->
<h2 id="topic-patterns">4. Recurring Topics &amp; Question Content Patterns</h2>

<p>To identify which concepts dominate the BIEK Computer Science exam, we performed a comprehensive keyword-frequency analysis across all 327 question texts. Each question was mapped to 14 thematic categories based on the presence of discipline-specific terminology.</p>

<div class="chart-box">
  <div class="chart-title">Topic Coverage Across All 327 Questions (Percentage of Questions Mentioning Each Topic)</div>
  <canvas id="chartTopicBars"></canvas>
</div>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Topic Category</th><th class="num">Questions</th><th class="num">Coverage</th><th>Dominant Question Type</th></tr></thead>
